src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:235:            No bidding or budget decision should precede conversion cleanup. The Search campaign currently uses Maximize Conversions, so every primary action can influence bidding. Counting newsletter registrations and soft engagement actions as success risks directing spend toward users most likely to take easy actions rather than become qualified Consulting opportunities.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:265:            Changing primary conversions will change Smart Bidding behaviour and reported CPA. Expect a learning and restabilisation period; do not interpret an immediate fall in reported conversions as lost business when easy actions have deliberately been removed.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:289:            The Search campaign is verified as using Maximize Conversions with no target CPA. It produced 26 reported conversions in the last 30 days, but only approximately 20 appear to be real leads. The current optimisation signal is polluted by four Newsletter Sign Ups plus soft actions.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:301:            The prescribed ads-budget rubric says: below 30 conversions/month, use Maximize Clicks with a CPC cap; between 30 and 50 conversions/month, use Maximize Conversions; and use tCPA only after stable CPA and greater conversion volume.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:307:            This conflict should not be resolved by automatically switching a mature campaign to Maximize Clicks. Maximize Clicks optimises traffic volume rather than lead quality and could amplify irrelevant demand before the resolved 30-day search-term evidence and existing negative inventory have been fully audited and extended with longer history.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:333:          label="E4 · Spend concentration and conditional rebalancing"
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:339:            Manual Handling Training represented 49% of the last-30-day Search spend. This concentration is directionally plausible because “manual handling training” is the dominant verified demand term at approximately 2,700 Australian searches per month. Concentration alone is not proof of waste.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:342:            Ergonomic Office Consulting generated seven reported conversions and the best observed reported cost-per-lead signal. That result is promising, but it is not yet a scale directive because the evidence does not show whether those conversions were genuine enquiries, qualified calls, newsletter registrations or other soft actions. Exact spend and CPA figures are detailed in the private PDF pack.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:346:            The 3× Kill Rule requires a business-approved target CPA. No target CPA or qualified-lead CAC ceiling has been supplied, so no ad group should be labelled for immediate pause from this evidence. Let T equal the approved clean target CPA.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:360:            For Manual Handling Training specifically, the diagnostic must separate query quality and lead quality before reallocation. Its large spend share may reflect genuine market demand, loose matching, weak negatives or some combination of the three. The 12 July keyword pull adds one refinement: <code>manual handling</code> PHRASE at QS=3 is in the rubric’s <strong>fail tier</strong>, while several QS=5 keywords are in its <strong>warning tier</strong>. Diagnose the Quality Score components rather than treating all core keywords alike.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:363:            Certificate intent also contains two cohorts: clearly individual leakage and a converting corporate/online slice. The term <code>manual handling certificate online australia</code> produced 1.33 reported conversions in the evidence set. <strong>Do not blanket-exclude</strong> certificate intent; use the complementary-controls decision table and the client-sign-off-required certificate block.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:366:            Separately, the generic competitor/generic ad group used 18.7% of spend, with 55 clicks and 4.5 reported conversions. Conversion quality for that group total is unverified. The live keyword pull shows it is not a Dynamic Search Ads group: it holds nine static EXACT keywords—six competitor-keyword entries across four competitors plus three generics. Only the sampled government/competitor-query subset was near-zero converting. The evidence gap is therefore whether the group-level reported conversions represent qualified demand and whether the sampled leakage warrants tighter query controls.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:370:            Scaling is permitted only after a segment meets its clean target CPA consistently for at least two weeks and shows stable lead quality. The skill rubric also uses at least 50 conversions per week as a full “green light” for scaling; ErgoWorks is far below that threshold at approximately 20 real leads per month. This account therefore does not qualify for unconditional scaling under that rule.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:384:            The best observed reported signal for Ergonomic Office Consulting makes it the first segment to validate for controlled expansion—not an automatic recipient of more spend.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:397:            The Brand ad group delivered zero spend, zero clicks and zero conversions in the last 30 days. Dedicated Brand routing and reporting are absent; service groups currently capture Brand queries.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:404:            The same pull adds a structural refinement: all three terms are ENABLED as duplicates inside five non-brand ad groups. Brand queries are therefore not unprotected—they are being captured by whichever service ad group wins the internal auction, served non-brand ads and non-brand landing pages, and reported inside service ad-group metrics. The repair is consolidation, not just re-enablement; a small portion of Manual Handling Training’s reported conversions may currently be brand-query conversions.
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:410:            <li>3. Verify Brand query routing and separate Brand/service metrics, then monitor delivery and spend for a full period.</li>
src/app/ergoworks/plan/audit/page.tsx:426:            Once delivery resumes, pull Brand search volume, search terms, auction insights, impression share and lost impression share by budget/rank before deciding repair-in-place versus campaign breakout.
